  "messages": {
    "m-2050-1": "Our clinic is on the second floor and the freight elevator is out of service until November. There are 22 steps with one landing, and I emailed photos of the stairwell and both turns. The stair carry sounds good, go ahead.",
    "m-2051-1": "Curbside is fine, we have a forklift and a loading door at the club. Please call the front desk before delivery.",
    "m-2052-1": "Gravel driveway, level all the way to the garage, no step or lip at the door. The garage door is 9 feet wide.",
    "m-1041-1": "Bike goes in the spare bedroom on the ground floor. Two steps up to the front door, then a straight hallway with one turn at the end. Narrowest door is the bedroom door, 30 inches. I already emailed photos of the path and the turn.",
    "m-1043-1": "It's for my dad, the machine goes in his bedroom upstairs. One flight of stairs, about 14 steps, with a landing halfway. The bedroom door is 30 inches wide.",
    "m-1044-1": "Leave it in the garage please. Heads up, the driveway is dirt and gravel mixed and gets soft when it rains, and there's a small lip at the garage door.",
    "m-1045-1": "Basement gym. Call me when it ships.",
    "m-1046-1": "Need this before our studio opens on October 10. Curbside is fine, we'll carry it in ourselves.",
    "m-1047-1": "You delivered my last treadmill on your own truck, so I'm expecting free local delivery again.",
    "m-1048-1": "Curbside is fine. Please text me before the driver arrives.",
    "m-1049-1": "Yes, go ahead with the two step thing, sounds good. Ground floor condo, one step at the entrance, doors are 32 inches. I'll send photos this weekend.",
    "m-1051-1": "Home office on the ground floor, no steps from the driveway. All doors are 34 inches. I sent photos of the hallway and the one turn.",
    "m-a-neg": "It is not going in the garage. It goes in the upstairs office, 16 steps up.",
    "m-a-corr": "The old form says three steps. That is wrong; there are twelve.",
    "m-a-unit": "The narrowest door is 32.",
    "m-a-unknown": "Not sure how many steps, maybe a few.",
    "m-a-conf-1": "Doorway is 30 inches.",
    "m-a-conf-2": "Correction, I measured again: the doorway is 28 inches.",
    "m-a-prelim": "Sounds good, go ahead with that."
  },
